---
title: "SD-09 Cancel a Running Job (UML Sequence Diagram)"
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as Developer
  participant API as api.RunsHandler
  participant S as scheduler.Service
  participant RA as runnerapi
  participant E as runner.Executor
  participant PG as procgroup.Group

  U->>API: POST /runs/97/cancel
  API->>S: CancelRun(actor, 97)
  S->>S: queued/waiting jobs → cancelled, running jobs → cancelling
  S-->>API: ok
  API-->>U: 202
  E->>RA: PATCH /jobs/812/log (next chunk or heartbeat)
  RA->>S: AppendLog(...)
  S-->>RA: cancel = true
  RA-->>E: 202 {cancel: true}
  E->>PG: Kill()
  alt Linux
    PG->>PG: SIGTERM to process group, wait 10 s, SIGKILL
  else Windows
    PG->>PG: TerminateJobObject (whole tree)
  end
  E->>RA: PUT /jobs/812/finish {status: cancelled}
  RA->>S: FinishJob(812, cancelled)
  S->>S: run status → cancelled
  Note over S: if the runner never answers, the reaper marks the job cancelled after 60 s
